### 2. Même email → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lucas@test.fr",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### 3. Mot de passe trop court → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "autre@test.fr",
  "password": "abc"
}

### 4. JSON invalide → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "cassé@test.fr", }

### 5. Confirmation → 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lucas@test.fr",
  "code": "665538"
}

### 6. Code faux → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lucas@test.fr",
  "code": "000000"
}

### 7. Connexion → 200 + token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lucas@test.fr",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### 8. Mauvais mot de passe → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lucas@test.fr",
  "password": "mauvais123"
}

### 9. Profil avec token → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Sans token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 11. Faux token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer nimportequoi